  "body": "## What changed\n\nThis PR adds the example catalog case `examples/catalog/turning/cone-thread`.\nThe case is a spun turning profile: a cone with a threaded end.\n\n- The stock is a 30 mm bar, 79 mm long.\n- The part has a collar, a 20 mm to 10 mm cone over 40 mm, an 8 mm neck and an M10x1.5 thread, 15 mm long.\n- The machine is the built-in `Lathe` (`assets/machines/lathe.mch`). The post is `Fanuc Lathe`.\n- The program has six operations: `Face`, `Rough profile`, `Finish profile`, `Neck`, `Thread`, `Part off`.\n\nThe case folder has the layout of #2393:\n\n- `model/gen_cone_thread_obj.py` and its two meshes\n- `build.camscript`\n- `cone-thread.camproj`\n- `cone-thread.nc`\n- `README.md`, which walks through the steps\n\nThe PR also adds one test to `crates/app/tests/example_catalog.rs` and the decision file `docs/decisions/2394-cone-thread.md`.\nNo file in `crates/*/src` changes.\n\n## Cause\n\nIssue #2394 asks for this case. The catalog infrastructure of #2393 is on `main` since v0.24.0.\n\n## Decisions that differ from the issue text\n\nThe decision file gives each one with its reason.\n\n- The case imports two models: the turned blank and the finished part. Profile Finish cannot finish the model that the Threading operation needs (#2880).\n- The neck needs a sixth operation, a Groove Finish. The issue lists five.\n- The thread posts as G32 passes, not as the G76 cycle. A G76 cycle would start inside the part (#2878, #2879).\n- The threading insert is a tool definition in the script. No catalog insert fits a 1.5 mm pitch (#893).\n- The shoulder has no fillet (#2881).\n\n## Bugs filed on the way\n\nThe issue says: \"Any refusal or wrong output found on the way is filed as its own bug and linked here.\"\n\n- #2878 (`P1`): a G76 cycle starts inside the part.\n- #2879 (`P3`): a threading pass cannot start in front of the end face.\n- #2880 (`P3`): Profile Finish reads thread valleys and a neck step as rest.\n- #2881 (`P3`): a steep fillet chord sends the profile ride far out of the bar.\n- #2882 (`P3`): the profile rides post runs of identical `G01` blocks. The committed program has 408 such blocks.\n\n## Tests\n\nPin: `example_catalog::turning_cone_thread_case_posts_the_taper_and_the_thread`. It reads the committed program and asserts:\n\n- the operation order,\n- the slope of each finish block on the cone (10 mm of diameter over 40 mm),\n- the G32 passes at lead 1.5, the last pass at the 8.16 mm root, the pass end at Z63.9,\n- the neck plunge to X8 and the part-off to X0.\n\nThe two suite tests that iterate all cases also cover the new case: `every_catalog_case_opens_regenerates_verifies_and_posts_byte_for_byte` and `every_catalog_case_rebuilds_from_camscript`.\n\nRed first: without the case folder the pin fails with `catalog case turning/cone-thread is missing`.\n\nMutations of the committed `.nc`, each restored after the run:\n\n| Mutation | Pin |\n|---|---|\n| case folder removed | red |\n| `G01 X10.212 Z58.4` changed to `X12.212` (taper) | red: `is off the taper: -0.141` |\n| `G32 Z63.9 F1.5` changed to `Z65.4` (thread end) | red: `each pass ends at the neck, Z63.9` |\n| files restored | green |\n\nThe first form of the taper assert let the taper mutation pass. The assert now checks each block on the cone.\n\nGates on the final head:\n\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`: green (`app:example_catalog`, whole suite, 16 s).\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n- `cargo xtask catalog --check`: `checked 2d/first-part`, `checked turning/cone-thread`.\n- `cargo xtask gate heavy --base upstream/main --dry-run`: the diff reaches no heavy lane.\n\n## Goldens moved\n\nNone. `git diff --stat upstream/main -- \"*.nc\" \"*.cl\"` shows one new file, `examples/catalog/turning/cone-thread/cone-thread.nc` (1197 lines). No file under `tests/golden/` changes.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- No machine or control simulator ran the program.\n- The lathe stock simulation does not cut threads. The verify verdict says so, and the thread is judged by its own operation verdict.\n- The tool holders are not judged: the tools have no modelled body.\n- `cargo xtask catalog --screenshots` and `--pdf` did not run.\n- The UI did not open the project.\n\n## Notes for the review\n\n- `cone-thread.camproj` is 1.5 MB. The seed case is 0.2 MB. The project holds two meshes and the toolpaths.\n- When #2882 is fixed, the committed `.nc` changes. That PR must rebuild the case.\n\n## Overlaps\n\n#2877 (draft, case `2d/contour-tabs`) touches the same file, `crates/app/tests/example_catalog.rs`, in a different function. The two PRs each add a new test function at the end of the file. Whichever merges second refreshes and keeps the two functions. The case folders do not overlap.\n\nChangelog: Examples: the catalog case `turning/cone-thread` shows a lathe job - a cone with an M10x1.5 threaded end (face, rough and finish profile, neck groove, thread, part-off) on the Fanuc lathe post.\n\nEffort: medium\n\nFixes #2394\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
